		{
			"id": "QyBEuxdN",
			"type": "text",
			"x": -295.1105511147212,
			"y": -244.87238006765563,
			"width": 990.2584245186257,
			"height": 150,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 0,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "a8",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 1897517836,
			"version": 166,
			"versionNonce": 444768308,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1783785759615,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Recursion is a programming technique where a method calls itself to solve smaller\ninstances of the same problem.\nTo understand it, we use the mathematical Factorial, denoted as n!. The factorial of 5 is\n5! = 5 x 4 x 3 x 2 x 1 = 120. \nMathematically, you can also write this as 5! = 5 x 4!. \nThis relies on itself to find the answer, which is the literal definition of recursion.  ",
			"rawText": "Recursion is a programming technique where a method calls itself to solve smaller instances of the same problem.\nTo understand it, we use the mathematical Factorial, denoted as n!. The factorial of 5 is 5! = 5 x 4 x 3 x 2 x 1 = 120. \nMathematically, you can also write this as 5! = 5 x 4!. \nThis relies on itself to find the answer, which is the literal definition of recursion.  ",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "Recursion is a programming technique where a method calls itself to solve smaller instances of the same problem.\nTo understand it, we use the mathematical Factorial, denoted as n!. The factorial of 5 is 5! = 5 x 4 x 3 x 2 x 1 = 120. \nMathematically, you can also write this as 5! = 5 x 4!. \nThis relies on itself to find the answer, which is the literal definition of recursion.  ",
			"autoResize": false,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
		{
			"id": "xjFZfwPl",
			"type": "text",
			"x": -286.1550728084789,
			"y": 479.37489324391487,
			"width": 950.2406790085735,
			"height": 50,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 0,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "a9",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 1079490956,
			"version": 1061,
			"versionNonce": 565542540,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1783785994032,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "When a computer runs a recursive method, it pauses the current method, saves its state\nin memory (the stack), and steps down to run the new method. ",
			"rawText": "When a computer runs a recursive method, it pauses the current method, saves its state in memory (the stack), and steps down to run the new method. ",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "When a computer runs a recursive method, it pauses the current method, saves its state in memory (the stack), and steps down to run the new method. ",
			"autoResize": false,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
		{
			"id": "KtM0emPU",
			"type": "text",
			"x": -288.3686495835097,
			"y": 787.0486128471612,
			"width": 943.7035566794016,
			"height": 25,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
