			"seed": 2109311796,
			"version": 493,
			"versionNonce": 267037492,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1783786911334,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "The Real-World Use Case: \nWe teach recursion using Factorials, but you would never actually use recursion for a\nsimple factorial in the real world (iteration is better for linear math). \nYou use recursion for branching structures like navigating a File System (a folder\ncontains folders, which contain folders) or traversing a Binary Search Tree (where\nevery node splits into two more nodes). \nManaging that with iterative loops requires building complex, manual Stack arrays.\nRecursion handles it automatically via the Call Stack.",
			"rawText": "The Real-World Use Case: \nWe teach recursion using Factorials, but you would never actually use recursion for a simple factorial in the real world (iteration is better for linear math). \nYou use recursion for branching structures like navigating a File System (a folder contains folders, which contain folders) or traversing a Binary Search Tree (where every node splits into two more nodes). \nManaging that with iterative loops requires building complex, manual Stack arrays. Recursion handles it automatically via the Call Stack.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": "7360NBc5",
			"originalText": "The Real-World Use Case: \nWe teach recursion using Factorials, but you would never actually use recursion for a simple factorial in the real world (iteration is better for linear math). \nYou use recursion for branching structures like navigating a File System (a folder contains folders, which contain folders) or traversing a Binary Search Tree (where every node splits into two more nodes). \nManaging that with iterative loops requires building complex, manual Stack arrays. Recursion handles it automatically via the Call Stack.",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
		{
			"id": "q7mmUIJU",
			"type": "text",
			"x": -290.95297045460234,
			"y": 3114.8022200894684,
			"width": 976.564682526789,
			"height": 125,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#e03131",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 1,
			"strokeStyle": "dashed",
			"roughness": 0,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "aH",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 1012644660,
			"version": 632,
			"versionNonce": 969921036,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1783786911334,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "- Memory Overheads: Recursion requires more memory space because every intermediate\ncalculation is stacked and held open in memory until the base case is reached.\n- Infinite Recursion: If you forget the base case (e.g., if (n == 1)), the method will\ncall itself forever. The computer will eventually run out of memory space on the Call\nStack and crash with a StackOverflowError.",
			"rawText": "- Memory Overheads: Recursion requires more memory space because every intermediate calculation is stacked and held open in memory until the base case is reached.\n- Infinite Recursion: If you forget the base case (e.g., if (n == 1)), the method will call itself forever. The computer will eventually run out of memory space on the Call Stack and crash with a StackOverflowError.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "- Memory Overheads: Recursion requires more memory space because every intermediate calculation is stacked and held open in memory until the base case is reached.\n- Infinite Recursion: If you forget the base case (e.g., if (n == 1)), the method will call itself forever. The computer will eventually run out of memory space on the Call Stack and crash with a StackOverflowError.",
			"autoResize": false,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false
		},
